Subject: Cantor Field Attention Reproducible Windows Build P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] a195b407-c8ad-4bd9-b11f-e405df534503
@ [source_manifest] C:\Project\Cantor\source_documents\2026-08-18_field_attention_reproducible_windows_build\Source_Document_Manifest.sop
@ [exploded_specification] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\exploded\Cantor_Field_Attention_Reproducible_Windows_Build_P0.exploded.sop
@ [canonical_specification] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\Cantor_Field_Attention_Reproducible_Windows_Build_P0.sop

& [Problem] is that FADL h8 has exact content identity but its build process was not shown to reproduce that identity

& [Decision] is a separately signed local proof profile over two clean archived source roots
  + exact Git identity prevents the dirty working tree from silently entering either build
  + separate source and target roots expose path and incremental-state sensitivity
  + SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH removes uncontrolled time input while remaining bound to source history
  + CARGO_INCREMENTAL zero prevents incremental cache state from entering the result
  + MSVC /Brepro requests deterministic linker output
  + locked offline Cargo prevents dependency resolution or network drift during the campaign
  + byte equality proves local artifact repetition while behavior checks guard against proving equality of the wrong executable

& [Alternatives] are bounded
  - rebuilding twice in one target directory is rejected because it can reuse outputs
  - two target directories under one mutable source tree are useful preliminary evidence but rejected as the final profile because source-path sensitivity remains hidden
  - comparing hashes alone is rejected because direct byte comparison is equally available
  - reproducing h8 retroactively is rejected because the original h8 build environment was not preserved under this profile
  - deploying the result is rejected because build repeatability and deployment authority are separate identities

& [RiskControl] keeps the proof tool subordinate to its evidence
  + temporary recursive cleanup is restricted to one validated target child
  + provider-facing commands are excluded so proof collection cannot create inference effects
  + stable receipts omit random temporary paths
  + any failed comparison or behavior check exits nonzero and withholds passed status

& [Nonclaim] is one host and toolchain establish local repeatability only
  + cross-machine reproduction remains a separate growth seed
  + protected signing and deployment trust remain separate work
  + this profile neither repairs nor replaces the historical h8 content identity
